  "summary": "An internal affairs report revealed that former Goodyear PD officer Kristopher Jackson used the department's Flock ALPR system to search a crime victim's license plate 36 times between January and February, turned off his body camera during a call with her, and ran her name through a state criminal database multiple times. Jackson resigned before the investigation concluded; Glendale PD investigated potential criminal charges but none were filed. The misuse was flagged by a routine Flock audit.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Thirty-six times between Jan. 4 and Feb. 8, Jackson searched the license plate belonging to the victim, including 14 times in one day.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "The department's internal affairs unit learned of the problem in July, when an internal affairs officer ran a Flock audit that flagged Jackson's searches.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "In August, an Apache Junction officer resigned after misusing Flock cameras to track his wife.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    }
  ],
